CONTEXT Migration IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Migration
{+ The migration system of the proof of concept in
"Data Migration under a Changing Schema in Ampersand" (RAMiCS 2024), written as a context
that includes the existing system as `old` and the desired system as `new`.
In 2024 the prefixes `old_` and `new_` were typed in by hand, in one script.
Here the two systems are the scripts they are in production, and the aliases supply the prefixes.

The numbers of the steps refer to section 4.1 of that paper. +}

INCLUDE "../contexts/kurk_existing.adl" AS old
INCLUDE "../contexts/kurk_desired.adl" AS new --# [ "Migrating" ]

-- Step 1. The data sets of both systems are both present, kept apart by the aliases.
-- The concepts of the two systems are different concepts. The migration states which ones correspond:
-- every atom of the existing system is an atom of the desired system.
CLASSIFY old.A ISA new.A
CLASSIFY old.B ISA new.B

-- Step 2. Copy the population of r. The relation copyR registers what has been copied,
-- so that a user can remove a copied pair from new.r without it being copied again.
RELATION copyR[old.A*old.B]
ENFORCE copyDone : copyR >: new.r /\ old.r
ENFORCE copy : new.r >: old.r - copyR

-- Step 3. For the new blocking invariant (r is total), fixedTotalR registers the atoms that satisfy it,
-- and a blocking invariant keeps a repaired violation from recurring.
RELATION fixedTotalR[new.A*new.A]
RULE blockTotalR : fixedTotalR |- new.r;new.r~
MEANING "An atom that has been paired with a B remains paired with a B."
MESSAGE "Relation r must remain total."
VIOLATION (TXT "Atom ", SRC I, TXT " must remain paired with an atom from B.")

-- Step 4. A transactional invariant produces the population of fixedTotalR.
ENFORCE fix : fixedTotalR >: I[new.A] /\ new.r;new.r~

-- Step 5. The new invariant as a business constraint, which signals what users have to repair.
RULE totalR : I[new.A] |- new.r;new.r~
MEANING "Every A is to be paired with a B."
MESSAGE "Please, make relation r total."
VIOLATION (TXT "Pair ", SRC I, TXT " with an (any) atom from B.")
ROLE User MAINTAINS totalR

-- Every atom of old.A is an atom of new.A, so new.r and fixedTotalR apply to it as well.
INTERFACE Migration FOR User : "_SESSION";V[SESSION*old.A] cRud BOX
  [ "A" : I cRud
  , "old r" : old.r cRud
  , "new r" : new.r CRUd
  , "fixed" : fixedTotalR cRud
  ]

ENDCONTEXT
